e. population administration and civil registration:f. women's empowerment, protection of women and children; g. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises; andh. public tranquility, public order, and community protection (2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

CHAPTER X

ADMINISTRATIVE SANCTIONS

Article 29

1. Any person who does not fulfill their obligations as referred to in Article 15 paragraph (2) and Article 16 shall be subject to administrative sanctions.
2. Administrative sanctions for persons as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:a. verbal warning;
b. written warning; and/or c. administrative fine (3) Administrative sanctions for persons as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of: - 14 -a. written warning;
b. temporary suspension of activities;
c. permanent cessation of activities;
d. temporary revocation of permit;
e. permanent revocation of permit; and/or f. administrative fine.
4. Administrative fines as referred to in paragraph (2) letter c and paragraph (3) letter f shall constitute Regional revenue.
5. Further provisions regarding the procedures for imposing administrative sanctions shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

Article 10

Regional Government conducts recovery as referred to in article 6 letter c, including:
a. providing physical recovery at health service institutions; b. providing medicolegal services;
c. assisting the repatriation of victims;
d. providing temporary protection in Safe Houses (safe house); e. providing psychosocial recovery and assistance;
f. providing spiritual guidance services; and/org. preparing family, school, work and community environment, as well as economic empowerment.

CHAPTER VIII

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 25

1. The Regional Government shall conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from violence.
2. Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) shall include: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. coordination;
d. monitoring;
e. evaluation; and f. reporting.

